<title>UK: Eight more banks to quote Swiss franc LIBOR - BBA.</title>
<headline>Eight more banks to quote Swiss franc LIBOR - BBA.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-09-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Eight more banks have agreed to contribute to the London Inter-bank Offered Rate (LIBOR) settlement panel for the Swiss franc, the British Bankers' Association (BBA) said in a statement.</p>
<p>The new panel members are Barclays Bank Plc, the Royal Bank of Scotland, the First National Bank of Chicago, Deutsche Morgan Grenfell, Bayerische Landesbank Girozentrale, Banque Nationale de Paris, ABN Amro Bank and Union Bank of Switzerland.</p>
<p>This will bring the size of the panel to 16.</p>
<p>Subject to market conditions, the additional banks will start quoting on October 15.</p>
<p>-- Rosemary Bennett, London Newsroom +44 171 542 7715</p>
</text>
